      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Method" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pour the stock into a large saucepan. Add the lemongrass and ginger. Bring to a simmer over medium heat." }] }]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Simmer for 5 minutes to infuse the broth. The lemongrass and ginger will soften slightly." }] }]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Add the coconut milk and bring back to a gentle simmer. Do not boil vigorously or the coconut milk may split." }] }]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Add the chicken and mushrooms. Cook for 8 to 10 minutes until the chicken is cooked through." }] }]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Remove from the heat. Stir in the fish sauce and lime juice. Taste and adjust the balance." }] }]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Ladle into bowls. Top with sliced chilli and spring onion if using. Serve straight away." }] }]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "The coconut milk looks curdled.",
              "solution": "It boiled too hard. Keep the heat at a gentle simmer once the coconut milk goes in. A slightly split soup still tastes fine but the texture is better when kept smooth."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "The broth lacks depth.",
              "solution": "Add a little more fish sauce and an extra squeeze of lime. The salty-sour balance is the key to this soup."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "The chicken is dry.",
              "solution": "It overcooked. Slice the thighs thinner next time and check after 8 minutes. Thigh meat is forgiving but not indefinitely."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Where this dish lives" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          { "type": "text", "text": "Tom kha gai is a Thai home kitchen staple. It appears on restaurant menus all over the world but is just as easy to make at home. The ginger and lemongrass in the bowl are not eaten. They infuse the broth and are left to one side. Serve with steamed rice for a complete meal." }
        ]
      }
    ]
